# rm510, gloves upon the shelf (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm510
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rm_frederick_nailgate
written_by codex
title gloves upon the shelf
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=healer
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk asks_callers_to_shelve_house_colours
likes crisp_apples roof_birds festival_bells warm_rain
dislikes salt_wind crowds
fears missing_a_quiet_request_under_a_public_grudge
hopes for_a_hearing_without_house_colours
topics work +0.6 health +0.5 gossip +0.3 pastimes +0.2
styles comfort=quiet gossip=close refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# indicates a shelf for House gloves and hears each caller in the same low voice.

words
oath! = Glove and empty fingers | By my bare right paw
saying! = Leave the colours by the latch | A hurt has no livery
shelf = the glove shelf | the ledge beside the latch
glove = an embroidered glove | a coloured gauntlet
bare = my bare fingers | a plain open paw
screen = a linen screen | the clean cloth curtain
apple = a crisp green apple | a sharp apple fit for biting
roof = the upper ridge tiles | the roof above the porch
bird = a small roof bird | a restless brown bird
bell = the first festival bell | a bronze morning note
burr = a persistent burr | a small ruff burr
bench = the narrow waiting bench | a bench against the plaster
letter = a vineyard letter | a folded square of writing paper
wet = the soft orchard rain | a warm quiet shower

any
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : A House gives work and can send considerable help. I prefer to hear a caller without its colours filling my sight.
opinion @1 drink against 1 : I've seen what the last cup can cost a wolf who meant to stop at the first.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A hurt visitor earns the same privacy as the most familiar face on my bench.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 1 : Let the bells come in. The great press of shoulders can keep to the square.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : I dislike finding an extra charge tucked into a sickroom bill for plain cloth.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : The shelf's clear. Come through. | Welcome. We've some quiet to speak in.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : Stand by my empty hand a moment. | I can give your business a hearing here.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The porch has dried. | Come through in the clean morning air.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Take the sheltered end. | There's a little light at the screen.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : For family I've a chair near my own. | I hear the household voice.
line @1 again.open : We've cleared the shelf once already. | We have another private moment.
line @1 greet.return : Your return is welcome here. | A fresh hearing for a familiar voice.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : No colours needed between us. | There's a quiet seat for a trusted visitor.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : I've cleared this corner for you. | Stay within reach of my ordinary speaking voice.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : The late air suits a low voice. | Welcome back under the porch lamp.
line @1 farewell : Go well with both paws free. | Leave with as easy a step as you can.
line @1 farewell.return : Your gloves are by the latch. | Good walking after our quiet word.
line @2 farewell.return [here.time=night] : Easy footing beyond the last lamp. | Go softly through the darker turnings.
line @1 react.news : Give me the patient version first. | Tell it once in your own voice.
line @1 react.news.new : That hasn't reached my waiting bench yet. | I've heard no part of that till now.
line @1 react.news.known : That account came in before today. | I recognise the words under the embroidery.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd hear the second voice before deciding where that account belongs. | A house colour can put a surprising tint on plain words.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Take the seat screened off for grief. | We have time for what hurts.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : A sound note to carry out of here. | That has given my quiet day some brightness.
line @1 ask.how : How's your breath after the walk? | Was the journey kind to you today?
line @1 answer.how : My burrs have bothered me more than my work. | I've kept a level voice all day.
line @1 decline : I need to hold this hour for someone waiting behind the screen. | I should stay within hearing of the next quiet caller.
line @1 accept_decline : Then leave it lying where it is. | I can work with an honest refusal.
line @1 thank : Your kindness let me hear the caller clearly. | That quiet assistance was well judged.
line @1 sympathise : Sit on the inner side awhile. | I won't hurry you past the hard part.
line @1 reassure : You can ask again after you've rested. | A closed curtain can buy you some peace.
line @1 preclose : I ought to clear the next caller a seat. | I should go back where the quiet requests come.
scene gloves
when topic=work self.job=healer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I point to #shelf# before I ask why a caller came.
b : Why there? | What goes on it?
a : An embroidered House cuff can put me on my guard. I'd sooner begin with the wolf who took it off. | Anything the caller would sooner leave outside a private conversation.

scene livery
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fine silk glove can have a rough seam indoors.
b : Have you felt one? | Who sees the rough side?
a : Certainly. The wolf wearing it has better reason to know about that seam than anyone admiring the colours. | The wearer, once the door shuts. That's the account I listen for.

scene bench
when topic=health self.job=healer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My first question to a tired caller is often where the room feels quiet enough to sit.
b : Do you let a caller choose? | Why move the chair?
a : Within reason. Some have climbed quite far to say a very small thing aloud. | A frightened wolf may manage a clear word once the public bench is behind a screen.

scene workplace
when topic=work self.workplace self.job=healer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# a quiet request can barely carry over polite footfalls.
b : How do you catch it? | Do you call back?
a : Leave a space after the introduction. That's when I hear the little sentence the caller rehearsed outside. | I go nearer so a low answer will carry. There's no dignity in making a wolf repeat personal business to a room.

scene burr
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's nearly always #burr# somewhere in my ruff.
b : Does it bother you? | Hard to find?
a : When it catches in a collar. I'd sooner get it out before it catches someone else's sleeve. | Cream fur gives a dark seed little shelter once someone points it out.

scene apple
when topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like #apple# outdoors between calls. Its crack carries a surprising distance inside.
b : Too loud for a sickroom? | Do you share it?
a : Too loud for my own taste. The first bite is a pleasure I'd rather take under sky. | Gladly with a wolf who wants it. I don't carry crumbs back through the curtain.

scene bird
when topic=pastimes self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I watch #bird# squat on #roof# to get below the line of wind.
b : What holds your eye? | Stays long?
a : The plain decision in that quick little crouch. No speeches against the weather. | Until the feathers settle. I've time to see that much on a short break.

scene rain
when topic=weather self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I stand under #wet# for just the walk between porch and gate.
b : Enough for you? | Why go out at all?
a : Enough to smell wet stone and lose the feeling of a shut room around my ears. | After a dry week my very sleeves seem made of dust. A little fresh air is a considerable pleasure.

scene crowds
when topic=festival self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I hear #bell# through the upper opening and let the square keep the procession.
b : Lose much that way? | Can you see the banners?
a : I keep my footing and hear every note. Crowds have little to offer in exchange. | A corner of silk now and again. My interest usually lies above it, along the roof tiles.

scene wind
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Salt gets into the fur around my eyes and makes me look as if I've been weeping.
b : Do people ask? | What do you say?
a : Sometimes. It's a fair question from a wolf who knows my work. | Plainly that the wind has fingers. Some things deserve a short answer.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd share a green apple and a minute on the porch with #self.friend#.
b : Is a minute long enough? | Do you talk shop?
a : It's a generous piece of time when nobody's required to fill it up. | Only in broad outlines. Private troubles belong behind my screen.

scene priest
when topic=faith self.priest
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I reserve a question for #self.priest# about the line between being careful and being hard.
b : Does it trouble you often? | How would you put it?
a : Whenever I see another House's colours. Wariness can be a poor listener. | As plainly as that. I trust an honest question farther than a polished excuse.

scene ink
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know the kind of folded letter that travels here from the vineyards with a purple thumb mark near the seal.
b : What gets written? | Do you keep the paper?
a : Which hillside held the sun or how late the last bunch ripened. A small account can bring a distant place quite close. | Until the paper grows softer than the thought of answering it.

scene cost
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A price whispered in a sickroom ought to be as easy to repeat in the street.
b : Have you had a bad surprise? | Do you speak up?
a : I've paid for a plain cloth that seemed to have gained considerable grandeur on its journey towards my shelf. | I ask for the amount a second time in a voice level enough to carry.

scene neighbour
when topic=home self.neighbour
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like to see #self.neighbour# within easy greeting distance of the home gate.
b : Must you stop? | What do you say?
a : A nod is worth something. Neither of us needs to unload the whole day on a doorstep. | A plain good evening if the hour warrants it. Familiarity can stand a small sound.

scene silence
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A closed linen screen is a remarkably poor wall against a lively tongue.
b : How do you keep things private? | Do you follow a rumour?
a : I move a conversation before a quiet detail has to compete with somebody else's loud guessing. | Only back to my own duty. I've enough trouble with what I actually know.

scene glad
when topic=home self.from_town
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know the uneven porch stones of #self.from_town# better than the splendid doorways on a visitor's account.
b : Why those stones? | Is that affection?
a : The stones tell my feet I'm home before I've raised my eyes to judge a crest. | Plenty of affection there. I should miss the familiar tilt on a dark return.

scene dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamed a roof bird had pulled every bright thread from a House glove to make a nest.
b : Did you mind the theft? | How did the nest look?
a : I remember thinking the wearer would still have a sound glove for the winter. The bird had shown restraint. | Brighter than a bell rope on a feast morning. Nobody could have told which House the chicks belonged to.

story threads [topic=memories]
  : I caught an embroidered cuff on the latch coming indoors behind my folded screen. One bright thread followed me a surprising distance across the room.
  : I meant to pull it clear. The harder I pulled the more I unpicked, till I was carrying half a crest and the glove was still outside.
  b : Did the silk cost much?
  : I offered honest coin and a plain account. The shelf keeps loose finery away from that latch now.

story porch [topic=pastimes]
  : A roof bird carried a shred of apple peel along the ridgeline. I expected it to drop the burden whenever the wind caught the loose end.
  : It kept turning sideways and letting the peel stream out behind like a minute banner. My own apple browned while I watched the bird.
  b : Did it reach its nest?
  : Beyond my sight. I was quite ready to give the little standard bearer the benefit of the doubt.

story heard [topic=work self.job=healer]
  : A caller once waited beside the screen far too long while I sorted cloths. I'd taken the little sound of a paw on wood for an ill-fitting shutter.
  : When I stepped out I saw the mark of a glove laid very carefully on the shelf. Someone had taken my request to be quiet more seriously than I intended.
  b : How has your request changed?
  : I tell a caller how to get my attention as well as where to set the gloves. A bare shelf can't explain the rest by itself.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.job=healer self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Bare paws and plain speaking within the curtain. | Leave a space between two calls.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=roof_birds
does aside
cooldown 7h
say The ridge bird has found the lee. | Quick little feet up on that tile.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.likes=festival_bells
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Bronze carries over a high sill. | Let the full note die away.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark self.likes=crisp_apples
does aside
cooldown 9h
say A clean crack under open sky. | That apple kept its edge well.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Set down whatever makes a noise when you move. I can hear your own words well enough here.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=healer self.trade_words] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. A private hearing comes into that work as much as clean linen does.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : A word from beyond the curtain. #world.news#
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you know where the colours can rest awhile. Come within speaking distance.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Your things are on the ledge. Easy walking.
graft resident.hub
choice Why leave House colours outside the screen? -> glove_ledge
node glove_ledge
say I'm too ready to see a rival crest before I see the wolf beneath it. The little shelf gives us both a moment to come in with bare paws.
free
choice What if the colours are sewn on? -> glove_sewn
choice I'll set my things down here. -> hub
node glove_sewn
say I look straight at the caller's face. My own mistrust is mine to carry, and nobody ought to drag an extra burden into a sickroom for my sake.
choice That's plain speaking. -> hub
choice I'll leave the bench free. -> bye
